  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Polygonatoside A may interact with the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14 through a series of target relationships. The compound is linked to CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which in turn is targeted by 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide and (+)-(5S,7R)-7-Ethoxy-12-Hydroxy-2-Oxo-20-Norabieta-1(10),8,11,13-Tetraene. These intermediates are all predicted to target the 26S proteasome subunit, indicating a potential pathway through which Polygonatoside A may influence proteasome function. The scores from the different paths are consistent, suggesting a plausible biological relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The evidence supports a possible role for Polygonatoside A in modulating proteasome activity, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and functional significance.",
